      "properties": {
        "OD1": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD1 \u2014 Source/domain admission | `Sequence::plan`, `FrameBindings`, projection before `stage::start` | What exact valid binding/domain/alias/schema judgments apply? Which local duty registry identities may be projected, including discharge-only incoming duties and await/R7 boundaries? Current predicates are not silently weakened. Supply exact admission ordering and supported domain; ordinary SC2 projection is not an admission proof. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD2": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD2 \u2014 Identity and predecessor carrier | Catalog's existing Program/Plan hashes, invocation ordinals, any future persisted Sequence | Existing stage identities are preserved verbatim. Specify any new source/plan/manifest/whole-prefix identity, canonical preimage, verification, origin, reopen and persistent parent rules. Local labels/array indices are only observations. No new sequence hash, proof lineage or authenticity follows from this design. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD3": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD3 \u2014 Errors and publication | `SequenceError`, failures during planning/stage calls/projection/lift/checked totals/export | Specify variants, exact public wire, diagnostic precedence, mutation/publication points and retained earlier observations/work. Existing original StageRejection envelopes/counters must remain available under their current contract; how a new envelope carries them is not defined by this ordinary author. No fabricated zero-attempt result or silent truncation is proposed. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD4": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD4 \u2014 Global resource envelope | `LogicalAllocation`, cumulative attempted/committed/remaining observations, output tables | Decide global preflight/enforcement, false/rejected/late-call charges, overflow, invocation/plan/output limits, adapter overhead and closure-reserve use. Existing per-action caps are not raised or borrowed. The proposed positive-trace equations are descriptive arithmetic, not adequacy or lifecycle enforcement evidence. Native DUST/service/proof/wall-time/resource controls retain their owners and historical counters. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD5": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD5 \u2014 Participant authority, consent and effects | Whole head/duty creation, source inputs, events, any authenticated successor | Supply required participant/source/intent authority and consent semantics. A shared key, transfer, ordinary local outcome or reviewer decision supplies no such authority. The product remains permissionless; project membership is not a source-language validity argument. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD6": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD6 \u2014 Head/ledger/phase semantics | Future native `Step`, failed Q after completed P, reserved/recovery paths | Specify actual phase-dependent effects, consumption, rejection/recovery and native/ledger correspondence. Ordinary local prefix retention does not decide transaction phase atomicity, rollback, ledger uniqueness or proof induction. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD7": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD7 \u2014 Private/persistent handoff and asynchronous evidence | Any reopened continuation, external callback or another process/party | Specify permitted witness/artifact ownership, disclosure, availability, origin/correlation/finality/consumption, late results and recovery. The proposed one-process raw StageEvent flow retains current local labels and is not an authenticated asynchronous outcome or isolated private handoff. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "OD8": {
          "allOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/contract"
            },
            {
              "properties": {
                "originalRequestVerbatim": {
                  "const": "| OD8 \u2014 Other operators | Shared-state schedule, split/join, atomic domain and external asynchronous branches | Supply each operator's actual rule and designated-owner judgments. This sequence has one active action and one local predecessor; it cannot accept a many-parent Join or concurrent head by merely listing it as the next invocation. Existing D1\u2013D5/RV1\u2013RV3 and unadopted SI1\u2013SI4 are not modified. |\n"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
